<title>USA: Fed adds temporary reserves via 5-, 14-day RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds temporary reserves via 5-, 14-day RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Thursday through five- and 14-day fixed system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokesman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts had said the Fed would add reserves through multi-day system repurchase agreements.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-1/4 percent, the Fed's target for the rate, at the time of the operations.</p>
<p>-- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679</p>
</text>
